\section{Limitations}
\label{app:limitations}

Our study uses a single architecture (OpenVLA-OFT with LoRA rank 32); full fine-tuning may alter the interaction between auxiliary heads and encoder optimization because all parameters update simultaneously, potentially changing the gradient flow dynamics we observe. All experiments are conducted in MuJoCo simulation on a single task suite (SafeLIBERO Level~I, 10 tasks drawn from LIBERO-Spatial); whether the normalization-dependent gradient flow effect generalizes to other task distributions remains open. LIBERO-Object, which involves different spatial constraints, does not provide ground-truth occupancy labels, preventing factorial comparison on that benchmark; generating synthetic labels is straightforward but was not pursued in the current study. Real-world deployment introduces additional sources of distributional shift that could interact differently with auxiliary head training dynamics. The benchmark contains only static obstacles; dynamic obstacle scenarios may induce time-varying distributions where auxiliary head dynamics behave differently. Our collision metric is binary (L1 displacement threshold $10^{-3}$), which does not capture collision severity or near-miss behavior; a continuous safety metric might reveal finer-grained differences between conditions. CKA measures linear representational similarity, which may miss nonlinear structure relevant to safety behavior. The factorial design uses $n{=}3$--$4$ seeds per cell, which limits statistical power for individual pairwise tests (post-hoc power $\approx$ 0.3--0.4 for the observed BN-row effect size); we report effect sizes as the primary inferential quantity rather than relying on $p$-values. Larger-scale replication would further strengthen conclusions. Cutoff conditions have 1--3 seeds, limiting temporal conclusions to preliminary observations. All auxiliary conditions use a fixed loss weight $\lambda_0{=}0.01$ with exponential decay; we did not sweep this hyperparameter, so the gradient flow effect may vary under different loss weight schedules.

