The Detach+LN ablation replaces BatchNorm2d with LayerNorm in the auxiliary head while retaining \texttt{stop\_gradient}. Under v1 (3 seeds), Detach+LN achieves CAR $0.765 \pm 0.023$; the v2 preliminary result ($n{=}1$, CAR $0.826$; Table~\ref{tab:main_results}) is consistent with the effect pattern (Section~\ref{sec:mechanism}): removing gradient flow mitigates safety degradation regardless of normalization choice. Additional v2 seeds are in progress for camera-ready.

